PDF VOICE READER - CHANGELOG
=============================

Date: 2026-10-15
Release Version: 1.0.3

1. Audio Focus Auto-Resume Bug Fix:
   - Resolved native issue in PlaybackForegroundService where external audio apps (e.g. Spotify, YouTube, Podcasts) playing and pausing would automatically trigger playback resume in PDF Voice Reader.
   - Abandoned audio focus on pause. Removed automatic resume on AudioManager.AUDIOFOCUS_GAIN.
   - Playback now strictly requires manual user action (tapping the play button).

2. Interstitial Ads on Back Press:
   - Fixed back press navigation in Reader and Fullscreen Listening screens to reliably trigger full-screen interstitial ads.
   - Handled both top-bar UI back buttons and Android hardware/gesture back events via BackHandler.

3. Action-Triggered Interstitial Ads:
   - Starting Audio: When user taps "Listen" in Reader or plays audio from a stopped/idle state, an interstitial ad is shown before audio starts.
   - Pausing Audio: When user pauses speech, playback is paused and an interstitial ad is shown.
   - Resuming Audio: When user resumes playback, an interstitial ad is shown before playback continues.
   - Stopping Audio: When user stops speech, playback stops and an interstitial ad is shown.
   - TTS Voice Selection: When user selects a TTS voice in Settings, the voice changes and an interstitial ad is displayed.
   - Added `showInterstitialOrContinue()` pipeline in AdService to guarantee smooth continuation of navigation and audio.

4. Settings Screen Privacy Disclosure:
   - Removed inaccurate "Advertising & Trackers: None (Zero Tracking)" row from Settings screen.

5. Readable Document File Restriction:
   - Restricted document picker strictly to supported document types (application/pdf, application/epub+zip, text/plain, text/markdown).
   - Removed generic wildcard (*/*) file picker filter.
   - Added validation check rejecting unsupported file types with a friendly alert guiding users to select .pdf, .epub, .txt, or .md documents.

6. Background Playback Back Exit Modal:
   - When the user presses the back button (top UI button or Android hardware/gesture back) while audio is playing or paused, a modal appears asking if they want to "Hear in Background" or "Stop Playing".
   - If the user selects "Hear in Background", audio continues in the background and the screen exits without showing an ad.
   - If the user selects "Stop Playing", speech audio is halted and an interstitial ad is displayed before exiting.

7. Remove Files from Library:
   - Added a delete button (trash icon) to both featured and standard document cards in the Library.
   - Added long-press gesture support to trigger the delete confirmation.
   - Prompts the user with a native confirmation alert before deleting.
   - Cleans up document metadata from SQLite and automatically halts playback if the removed document was currently playing.

8. Interactive Word-Level & Paragraph Tap-to-Read:
   - Fixed paragraph tapping to resume reading from that paragraph.
   - Implemented tokenized word-level interactive touch targets in the Ebook/Text view: tapping any individual word starts reading aloud directly from that exact word.
   - Added custom character offset slicing and start-position synchronization in SpeechOrchestrator (`jumpToPosition`).

9. Full PDF View with Top Scrollable Page Selector:
   - Opening PDF view automatically jumps to the page currently being read out loud.
   - Added a horizontal scrollable bar of page chips at the top of the PDF view.
   - Clearly marks the selected page and displays a 🎧 reading badge on the page currently being read by TTS.
   - Tapping any page chip immediately navigates to that page in the PDF reader.

10. Persistent Home Screen Audio Player Controls:
    - Added a mini-player controller directly to the Home / Library screen tagged to the active or most recent document.
    - Displays document title, reading page status, and controls: Previous Track, Play/Pause, Next Track, and Stop.
    - If no document is active or library is empty, gracefully disables controls with contextual guidance ("Tap any PDF to start reading" or "Add a PDF to start reading").

11. Light Mode Default & Dark Mode Toggle:
    - Configured Light Mode as the default visual appearance of the app.
    - Added an interactive Dark Mode toggle switch and segmented mode selector (☀️ Light Mode vs 🌙 Dark Mode) to the Appearance section in Settings.
    - Persisted the user's theme selection across app restarts via AsyncStorage.

13. Interactive TTS Voice Previews:
    - Added dedicated live audio preview buttons (▶ Preview / ❚❚ Stop) to both the Settings voice picker modal and the First-Time Onboarding wizard.
    - Allows users to listen to live spoken audio from any installed native TTS voice before selecting.
    - Preview audio plays without triggering ads; confirming voice selection triggers an interstitial ad.

14. Engaging Multi-Step First-Time Setup Walkthrough:
    - Revamped app/welcome.tsx into a 4-step interactive setup wizard:
      * Step 1 (Appearance): Interactive Light Mode (Default) and Dark Mode cards with real-time live UI theme updates.
      * Step 2 (TTS Voice Selection): Interactive list of installed native voices with live audio previews and radio selection.
      * Step 3 (Default Reading Speed): Speed preset chips (0.75x to 2.0x) paired with an interactive "🔊 Test Speed Sample" audio sample button.
      * Step 4 (Supported Documents & Privacy): Comprehensive overview of supported formats (.pdf, .epub, .txt, .md) and 100% on-device offline guarantees.

15. Settings Appearance UI Simplification:
    - Cleaned up the Appearance section in Settings by removing redundant segmented pill buttons.
    - Retained the clean, standard Dark Mode switch toggle.

16. Language Filtering for Narrator Voice Selection:
    - Added horizontal scrollable language filter chips (All, English, Hindi, Spanish, French, German, Russian, Japanese, etc.) to 'Pick Your Narrator' in both First-Time Setup (app/welcome.tsx) and Settings (app/settings.tsx).
    - Dynamically computes voice counts per language badge and filters voices instantly upon tapping any language chip.
    - Enhanced voice previews to synthesize natural, native-script audio sample phrases tailored to the chosen language (e.g. Hindi preview: "नमस्ते! मैं आपके दस्तावेज़ स्पष्ट और स्वाभाविक आवाज़ में पढ़ने के लिए तैयार हूँ।", Spanish preview: "¡Hola! Estoy listo para leer tus documentos...", English preview: "Hello! I am ready to read your documents...").

17. Per-Document Language Detection & Narrator Voice Setup:
    - Built zero-dependency, 100% on-device language detector analyzing Unicode script ranges (Devanagari/Hindi/Marathi, Cyrillic/Russian, Arabic/Urdu, Japanese Kana, Korean Hangul, Tamil, Telugu, Bengali, Gujarati, etc.) and Latin stopword n-gram distributions.
    - When adding any document, page 0 text is automatically inspected and its language is detected without sending any data to external servers.
    - Launches a dedicated 'Document Narrator Setup' modal (DocumentVoiceSetupModal) presenting the auto-detected language, selectable override language chips, and filtered narrator voices matching that document's language with live audio previews.
    - Saves document-specific voice_id and language in SQLite database (with safe, idempotent schema migrations) and application state.
    - Updated SpeechOrchestrator to prioritize the document's selected voice during playback, allowing different documents (e.g. a Hindi document vs an English book) to read with their respective chosen narrators without altering the global default voice.
    - Added a [🎙️ Voice] action button in the Reader top navigation bar allowing users to change the document's narrator voice and language at any time.
